ksnip-pyqt6 (0.2.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
  * Add the Model Manager dialog. Packaged builds show a notice and disable
    pip-based installs because they do not ship a Python interpreter.
  * Fix the Windows startup crash caused by os.getuid(), show the main window
    normally, and scan the packaged executable with Microsoft Defender.
  * Keep the no-image window compact and collapse it back to the toolbar-only
    strip even after leaving a maximized editor.
  * Remember the last directory used by Open and Save, including the folder of
    the last saved or opened image.
  * Add a separate checkbox to remember the last opened image directory.
  * Match the Number tool badge to the Number Pointer (filled, bordered, more padding).
  * Reset transient tool state when switching tools so Select works after Number Pointer.
  * Share one badge font across Number, Number Pointer and Number Arrow.
  * Make the number badge margin configurable from Annotator settings (−2 to 40 px).
  * Expose the number badge margin in the annotation properties toolbar too.
  * Let Crop and Cut start over an existing annotation instead of grabbing it.
  * Give Crop a four-handle selection that applies with Enter or a double-click.
  * Exclude the mouse cursor by default and bake it into the image when enabled.
  * Tear down the full-screen selection overlay before showing the editor, so
    no leftover piece of the capture tool stays on screen.
  * Document the Windows external OCR setup and support .bat/.cmd scripts.
  * Add a --smoke-test path that starts Qt and constructs the main window, and
    run it on the portable and installed Windows artifacts.

 -- wachin <wachin.id@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

ksnip-pyqt6 (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
  * Add CI packaging for the AppImage, .deb, macOS portable ZIP, Windows
    portable ZIP and NSIS installer, published to GitHub Releases.
  * Keep QtDBus optional so the application starts on Windows and macOS.
  * Refresh the Debian packaging for a clean pybuild and lintian build.

 -- wachin <wachin.id@gmail.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

ksnip-pyqt6 (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of the PyQt6 port of ksnip.
  * Capture modes: rectangular area, last area, all screens, current screen,
    active window, window under the cursor and desktop portal.
  * Annotation editor with tabs, undo/redo, per-item rotation, stickers,
    watermark, spell checking and OCR.
  * Export to PNG, JPEG, BMP, TIFF and SVG, clipboard, printing and
    configurable upload scripts.

 -- wachin <wachin.id@gmail.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:38:53 -0500
